WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.117
In this video, you will change your contest after you have created it: the dates, the name, the message, the prize, and the rules.

00:00:08.117 --> 00:00:10.827
Plans change, and the site is built for that.

00:00:10.827 --> 00:00:12.005
We start on the map.

00:00:12.907 --> 00:00:16.969
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:16.969 --> 00:00:19.094
That is the only address you need.

00:00:21.584 --> 00:00:23.573
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:23.573 --> 00:00:26.666
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:27.771
Tap Use my location.

00:00:29.603 --> 00:00:32.326
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:32.326 --> 00:00:34.293
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:34.293 --> 00:00:37.091
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.295
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:43.295 --> 00:00:44.490
See the three dots?

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:48.793
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:48.793 --> 00:00:49.331
Tap them.

00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:53.431
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:53.431 --> 00:00:58.769
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:01:00.503 --> 00:01:01.086
Tap Mine.

00:01:01.086 --> 00:01:02.717
This is your personal page.

00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:08.076
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:09.796 --> 00:01:11.842
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:15.513
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:17.421 --> 00:01:20.269
Plans change, and you can change your contest at any time before you announce winners.

00:01:20.269 --> 00:01:23.051
On the Overview, find Schedule, which shows when entries close and when voting runs.

00:01:23.051 --> 00:01:23.608
Tap Change dates.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:30.172
Here you can move the day entries close, the day voting starts, and the day voting ends.

00:01:30.172 --> 00:01:33.604
Voting should start after entries close, and end after it starts.

00:01:33.604 --> 00:01:37.192
If you need more time for neighbors to enter, move these dates later.

00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:45.725
Scroll down and you can also change the contest name, the welcome message, the prize, and the official rules.

00:01:45.725 --> 00:01:47.691
Neighbors see the changes right away.

00:01:48.592 --> 00:01:50.786
When you are done, tap Save changes.

00:01:50.786 --> 00:01:57.488
Everyone on your team is emailed about the change, so nobody is surprised, and you have a record of what changed.

00:01:59.456 --> 00:02:00.970
Next up: Run voting.
